  "question": {
    "text": "A parallel plate capacitor has plate area <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> and plates separation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi></math>. The space between the plates is filled with a dielectric medium of a thickness <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi></math> and dielectric constant <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math>. The capacitance of the system is:"
  },
